{
  "summary": "Mask sensitive configuration options loaded from `settings.json` when logging startup arguments in `ArgsManager::LogArgs`. Keys in `m_settings.rw_settings` are parsed with `InterpretKey` to look up their argument flags and replace their logged value with `****` if flagged `SENSITIVE`.",
  "problem": "Sensitive settings such as `rpcpassword`, `rpcauth`, or `torpassword` provided via command-line arguments or `bitcoin.conf` are masked when logged, but options read from `settings.json` (`rw_settings`) are printed in cleartext to `debug.log` and stdout during node initialization.",
  "evidence": [
    "\"`ArgsManager::LogArgs` masks `SENSITIVE` options from `bitcoin.conf` and the command line via `logArgsPrefix`, but prints `m_settings.rw_settings` values verbatim. Secrets such as `rpcpassword`, `rpcuser`, `rpcauth`, or `torpassword` stored in `settings.json` are therefore written in cleartext to `debug.log` and startup console output.\" (PR description)",
    "Diff in `src/common/args.cpp` directly confirms `m_settings.rw_settings` previously logged `setting.second.write()` with no flag checks, now checks `*flags & SENSITIVE`."
  ],
